<title>POLAND: Polish yr/yr PPI 10.5 pct in Feb vs 11.0 Jan.</title>
<headline>Polish yr/yr PPI 10.5 pct in Feb vs 11.0 Jan.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish producer prices rose 0.6 percent in February against a 1.8 percent rise in January, taking year-on-year producer price inflation down to 10.5 percent, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>It said PPI rose 2.4 percent in the January-February period, compared with a 2.6 percent rise in the corresponding period last year.  </p>
<p> POLISH PRODUCER INFLATION	  FEB 97    JAN 97    FEB 96</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)	     0.6   1.8(1.9)	1.2</p>
<p> yr/yr change (pct)		    10.5  11.0(11.2)    13.8</p>
<p> manufacturing m/m change	     0.7   0.6(0.8)	0.9</p>
<p> manufacturing yr/yr change	   9.7   9.7(9.9)     13.4</p>
<p> mining m/m change			0.3   2.0(2.8)	0.8</p>
<p> mining yr/yr change		   13.8  14.7(15.6)    12.5</p>
<p> utilities m/m change		   0.3   8.0(7.9)	3.2</p>
<p> utilities yr/yr change		11.3  14.6(14.5)    19.1</p>
<p>NOTE: January figures are revised. Previously released data in brackets. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
